        |   / filter the list by name, workspace or cwd, incrementally as you type;    |[K
        |     Enter keeps the filter applied and returns the keymap to the (now        |[K
        |     narrowed) list, Esc clears it back to the full list; this is also the    |[K
        |     only route to an archived session (A), which is hidden from the          |[K
        |     default list entirely -- type enough of its name, workspace or cwd to    |[K
        |     match it and it appears like any other row, and U there unarchives it    |[K
        |   space move to the next session needing attention (waiting or error),       |[K
        |     wrapping around; does nothing when nothing needs attention and never     |[K
        |     changes any session's status                                             |[K
        |   c toggle the selected row's workspace group collapsed/expanded             |[K
        |   g / G jump to the first / last visible row                                 |[K
        |   , open/close settings (edit config.toml's keys); Esc closes, prompting to  |[K
        |     discard if there are unsaved changes                                     |[K
        |   t open/close the theme picker; previews live on the real session list,     |[K
        |     Enter selects, Esc reverts byte-for-byte                                 |[K
        |   | cycle the layout mode: auto → side-by-side → stacked → collapsed →       |[K
        |     auto; a chosen mode is pinned regardless of terminal width until you     |[K
        |     cycle again or the terminal cannot hold its floors, when deck falls      |[K
        |     back to auto without forgetting the pin                                  |[K
        |   < / > shrink/grow the sidebar by one column                                |[K
        |   ? open/close help; Esc closes help                                         |[K
        |   q or Ctrl+C quit deck                                                      |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Create dialog fields                                                         |[K
        |   Name                the display name; also the source of the tmux slug     |[K
        |   Working directory    the session's cwd; must exist and be a directory      |[K
        |   Agent               shell, claude, or pi; which adapter launches it        |[K
        |   Permission profile  how much the agent may do without asking (safe, plan,  |[K
        |                       edits, yolo); an unsupported profile for the chosen    |[K
        |                       agent degrades visibly instead of silently             |[K
        |   Launch args         extra argv appended after the adapter's own argv       |[K
        |   Env                 session-level environment variables (highest priority  |[K
        |                       in PATH resolution)                                    |[K
        |   Pre-launch command  runs in the pane before the agent starts; the SPEC's   |[K
        |                       intended use is loading secrets into the pane's        |[K
        |                       environment without deck ever storing or logging them  |[K
        |   Login shell         run the pane via $SHELL -lc instead of execing the     |[K
        |                       agent argv directly                                    |[K
        |   ↑/↓ changes field; Enter advances or submits; Esc cancels                  |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Yolo is gated by allow_yolo: it must be enabled in config.toml, or yolo is   |[K
        | not offered at all (the UI states why). Once allow_yolo is enabled, choosing |[K
        | yolo -- at create time or when switching profile with P -- takes effect      |[K
        | immediately, with no separate confirm keystroke. yolo_default (also          |[K
        | config.toml, default false) opens the create modal already on yolo once      |[K
        | allow_yolo is also enabled; with allow_yolo disabled it is inert, and        |[K
        | settings says so on its own row rather than silently ignoring it. In yolo,   |[K
        | permission prompts never fire, so the waiting column goes quiet for that     |[K
        | session -- attention then comes only from questions/needs-input              |[K
        | notifications, not from waiting; this is expected, not deck failing to       |[K
        | notice, and is worth remembering now that yolo_default can put a brand new   |[K
        | session there without the user ever having chosen yolo by hand.              |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Settings takeover (opened with ,)                                            |[K
        |   Tab or Left/Right      switch focus between the category list and the      |[K
        |                          field list                                          |[K
        |   Up/Down or j/k         move within the focused list                        |[K
        |   Enter or Space         toggle/cycle the focused field's value              |[K
        |   + / -                  adjust a bounded-integer field                      |[K
        |   /                      fuzzy-search every field by label or description    |[K
        |   Ctrl+S                 save staged edits to config.toml                    |[K
        |   Esc                    close; with unsaved changes, prompts to discard     |[K
