        up/down - n new - , settings - ? help - q quit[K[260;H[H+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+[K
        | deck help                                                                    |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Keys                                                                         |[K
        |   ↑/↓ or j/k select a session; as the selection settles (coalesced           |[K
        |     against DECK_PREVIEW_MS, not once per row while a key is held),          |[K
        |     deck also fits the newly selected session's window to the preview        |[K
        |     panel -- [ui] preview_fit, on by default -- the same cost Enter below    |[K
        |     pays at entry: a SIGWINCH, and scrollback consumed faster while the      |[K
        |     window is narrower than usual. Skipped below the interactive floor       |[K
        |     (never resizes into a box too small to be worth it, and never            |[K
        |     enters interactive mode as a side effect); best-effort, so a session     |[K
        |     an attached client is also watching simply keeps that client's own       |[K
        |     size the next time it redraws. preview_fit = false turns this off        |[K
        |     and leaves a session cropped bottom-left instead. While ? help, E the    |[K
        |     event log or i the detail view covers the list, these same keys          |[K
        |     instead scroll that overlay's own content by exactly one line per        |[K
        |     press, leaving the session selection where it was                        |[K
        |   PgUp/PgDn page up/down through the list, one page at a time; while ?       |[K
        |     help, E the event log or i the detail view covers the list, the          |[K
        |     same keys instead page that overlay's own content once it grows          |[K
        |     taller than the frame -- a whole page per press, so consecutive          |[K
        |     pages share no line; ↑/↓ or j/k there move one line at a time, and       |[K
        |     with mouse reporting on a wheel notch over the overlay does the same     |[K
        |   Enter enter interactive mode on the selected running session: keystrokes   |[K
        |     forward to its live pane exactly as a real attached client's would,      |[K
        |     until Ctrl+Q leaves and returns the terminal to this list; entering      |[K
        |     resizes the agent's window to fit the preview panel, and output the      |[K
        |     agent produces while that window is narrower than its usual size         |[K
        |     consumes its own scrollback faster than the same output would at         |[K
        |     full width; while interactive, a wheel notch or Shift+PgUp/PgDn          |[K
        |     scrolls this bounded, deck-owned scrollback of the fitted view (not      |[K
        |     the pane's own tmux scrollback) rather than forwarding to the pane;      |[K
        |     typing snaps the view back to the live bottom                            |[K
        |   a attach the selected running session (full-screen, like Ctrl+Q never      |[K
        |     happened -- Enter enters interactive mode instead)                       |[K
        |   Y acknowledge the selected waiting/error session, clear its unseen marker  |[K
        |   n create a session (shell, or an agent: claude or pi)                      |[K
        |   x kill the selected running session; a toast naming undo stays visible     |[K
        |     for DECK_UNDO_MS afterward                                               |[K
        |   u undo the most recent x within its DECK_UNDO_MS window: resumes that      |[K
        |     session with its own resume argv, exactly like r; once the window has    |[K
        |     expired, or nothing has been killed since the last undo, it does nothing |[K
        |   dd delete the selected session: the first d shows a pending indicator and  |[K
        |     changes nothing; Esc or any other key cancels it; the second d opens a   |[K
        |     confirm dialog naming what survives -- the conversation and its working  |[K
        |     directory are never touched; the dialog also offers a non-default        |[K
        |     purge choice naming the exact transcript path it will delete, or         |[K
        |     declining when the agent has none to locate; Enter kills the live pane   |[K
        |     (if any) and tombstones the row, which disappears from the list          |[K
        |     immediately; a toast naming undo stays visible for DECK_DELETE_GRACE_MS  |[K
        |     afterward -- u within that window restores the row (deleted_at           |[K
        |     cleared, back in the list); once the window expires the row is reaped    |[K
        |     and u does nothing                                                       |[K
        |   A archive the selected session, hidden from the default list from then     |[K
        |     on: a confirm dialog opens first, naming the session -- and, on a row    |[K
        |     that is not stopped, saying that confirming does "kill and archive" as   |[K
        |     a single action rather than refusing the keypress the way x refuses an   |[K
        |     already-stopped row; nothing is written until you confirm;               |[K
        |     archived_at is a flag, never a status, so the row keeps whatever status  |[K
        |     it had; U below is the way back                                          |[K
        |   U unarchive the selected archived row: clears archived_at so the row       |[K
        |     returns to the default list, keeping whatever status it had (a session   |[K
        |     killed on its way into the archive comes back stopped -- r resumes it    |[K
        |     as a separate step). Reachable from inside the / filter's results,       |[K
        |     which is where an archived row is found in the first place: type enough  |[K
        |     of its name to surface it, Enter to keep the filter applied, then U      |[K
        |   m toggle a mark on the selected session (kept by session id, so it         |[K
        |     survives a re-sort or re-group); with the mark set non-empty, x and dd   |[K
        |     act on the whole batch instead of just the selected row, and ONE u       |[K
        |     restores the entire batch in one action; the marks clear on that         |[K
        |     action and on Esc                                                        |[K
        |   r resume the selected stopped session with its own agent argv (never       |[K
        |     --continue or "most recent"); resumed agents read "starting - awaiting   |[K
        |     signal" until a hook or sampled probe reports ready, while live shells   |[K
        |     become "running" on reconciliation; a client that loses the launch-lease |[K
        |     race sees "starting elsewhere" instead of an error                       |[K
        |   R restart the selected non-stopped session: kills its live pane if one     |[K
        |     exists and relaunches it with the same resume argv and conversation id   |[K
        |     (never a fresh conversation); this is the only action that applies a     |[K
        |     pending env↻ edit to the new pane and clears env↻ once it is up          |[K
        |   P switch the permission profile of the selected session; only takes        |[K
        |     effect on the next launch or resume ("restart to apply"), never the      |[K
        |     live pane                                                                |[K
        |   p pin the selected session's conversation id so future resumes always      |[K
        |     reuse it, or launch a one-shot fresh conversation (reverts to normal     |[K
        |     auto-resume afterward, it does not stay pinned or cleared)               |[K
        |   i toggle detail view for the selected session; r inside it renames the     |[K
        |     session's display name only -- the tmux session keeps its own name       |[K
        |     (deck_<slug>), never renamed, so a rename can never move or disturb a    |[K
        |     live pane's identity                                                     |[K
        |   e open the env editor for the selected session: every key deck resolved a  |[K
        |     layer for, its effective value, and which layer won -- server env,       |[K
        |     captured_path, config [env] or session env (SPEC §6.1/§6.3); j/k select  |[K
        |     a key, Enter edits its value, typing then Enter saves it into the        |[K
        |     session's own env and marks it env-dirty until a later restart picks     |[K
        |     it up; the save mirrors into tmux's own environment for future panes,    |[K
        |     never into whatever the pane's already-running process started with;     |[K
        |     secret-shaped keys mask by default (§6.4); r toggles reveal, resets on   |[K
        |     reopen; Esc cancels an edit in progress, or closes the dialog otherwise  |[K
        |   E open/close the event log: every recorded event across every session --   |[K
        |     kind, reason, a bounded payload -- newest first; a payload's             |[K
        |     secret-shaped values mask the same way the env editor's do; Esc closes   |[K
        |   / filter the list by name, workspace or cwd, incrementally as you type;    |[K
        |     Enter keeps the filter applied and returns the keymap to the (now        |[K
        |     narrowed) list, Esc clears it back to the full list; this is also the    |[K
        |     only route to an archived session (A), which is hidden from the          |[K
        |     default list entirely -- type enough of its name, workspace or cwd to    |[K
        |     match it and it appears like any other row, and U there unarchives it    |[K
        |   space move to the next session needing attention (waiting or error),       |[K
        |     wrapping around; does nothing when nothing needs attention and never     |[K
        |     changes any session's status                                             |[K
        |   c toggle the selected row's workspace group collapsed/expanded             |[K
        |   g / G jump to the first / last visible row                                 |[K
        |   , open/close settings (edit config.toml's keys); Esc closes, prompting to  |[K
        |     discard if there are unsaved changes                                     |[K
        |   t open/close the theme picker; previews live on the real session list,     |[K
        |     Enter selects, Esc reverts byte-for-byte                                 |[K
        |   | cycle the layout mode: auto → side-by-side → stacked → collapsed →       |[K
        |     auto; a chosen mode is pinned regardless of terminal width until you     |[K
        |     cycle again or the terminal cannot hold its floors, when deck falls      |[K
        |     back to auto without forgetting the pin                                  |[K
        |   < / > shrink/grow the sidebar by one column                                |[K
        |   ? open/close help; Esc closes help                                         |[K
        |   q or Ctrl+C quit deck                                                      |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Create dialog fields                                                         |[K
        |   Name                the display name; also the source of the tmux slug     |[K
        |   Working directory    the session's cwd; must exist and be a directory      |[K
        |   Agent               shell, claude, or pi; which adapter launches it        |[K
        |   Permission profile  how much the agent may do without asking (safe, plan,  |[K
        |                       edits, yolo); an unsupported profile for the chosen    |[K
        |                       agent degrades visibly instead of silently             |[K
        |   Launch args         extra argv appended after the adapter's own argv       |[K
        |   Env                 session-level environment variables (highest priority  |[K
        |                       in PATH resolution)                                    |[K
        |   Pre-launch command  runs in the pane before the agent starts; the SPEC's   |[K
        |                       intended use is loading secrets into the pane's        |[K
        |                       environment without deck ever storing or logging them  |[K
        |   Login shell         run the pane via $SHELL -lc instead of execing the     |[K
        |                       agent argv directly                                    |[K
        |   ↑/↓ changes field; Enter advances or submits; Esc cancels                  |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Yolo is gated by allow_yolo: it must be enabled in config.toml, or yolo is   |[K
        | not offered at all (the UI states why). Once allow_yolo is enabled, choosing |[K
        | yolo -- at create time or when switching profile with P -- takes effect      |[K
        | immediately, with no separate confirm keystroke. yolo_default (also          |[K
        | config.toml, default false) opens the create modal already on yolo once      |[K
        | allow_yolo is also enabled; with allow_yolo disabled it is inert, and        |[K
        | settings says so on its own row rather than silently ignoring it. In yolo,   |[K
        | permission prompts never fire, so the waiting column goes quiet for that     |[K
        | session -- attention then comes only from questions/needs-input              |[K
        | notifications, not from waiting; this is expected, not deck failing to       |[K
        | notice, and is worth remembering now that yolo_default can put a brand new   |[K
        | session there without the user ever having chosen yolo by hand.              |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Settings takeover (opened with ,)                                            |[K
        |   Tab or Left/Right      switch focus between the category list and the      |[K
        |                          field list                                          |[K
        |   Up/Down or j/k         move within the focused list                        |[K
        |   Enter or Space         toggle/cycle the focused field's value              |[K
        |   + / -                  adjust a bounded-integer field                      |[K
        |   /                      fuzzy-search every field by label or description    |[K
        |   Ctrl+S                 save staged edits to config.toml                    |[K
        |   Esc                    close; with unsaved changes, prompts to discard     |[K
        |                          (y/Enter discards, any other key keeps editing)     |[K
        |   [env] entries editor: - removes an entry, r reveals/masks secret-shaped    |[K
        |                          values (SPEC §6.4, resets to masked on reopen)      |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Theme picker (opened with t)                                                 |[K
        |   Left/Right or Up/Down or Space   change the previewed theme                |[K
        |   Enter                  select the previewed theme and save it              |[K
        |   Esc                    revert to the theme active before the picker opened |[K
        |                                                                              |[K
        | Runtime controls                                                             |[K
        |   DECK_HOME             isolated data/config/state root                      |[K
        |   DECK_TMUX_SOCKET      private tmux socket (default: deck)                  |[K
        |   DECK_CLOCK            freeze wall clock (RFC3339); clock.now overrides it  |[K
        |   DECK_CLOCK_STEP       exact amount advanced by each on-demand trigger      |[K
        |   Trigger             kill -USR1 <deck-client-pid>; each invocation advances |[K
        |                         the shared clock by exactly DECK_CLOCK_STEP          |[K
        |   clock.now             shared RFC3339 state under the resolved data root;   |[K
        |                         the trigger updates it and every process reads it    |[K
        |   DECK_ID_SEED          deterministic generated UUIDs                        |[K
        |   DECK_RECONCILE_MS     list/reconciliation interval in milliseconds         |[K
        |   DECK_PREVIEW_MS       pane-preview interval in milliseconds                |[K
        |   DECK_UNDO_MS          undo
